| !Run for !ClassiCube (RISC OS port)
Set ClassiCube$Dir <Obey$Dir>
IconSprites <ClassiCube$Dir>.!Sprites
|
| UnixLib and GCC 10's support module (both from PackMan)
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 RMLoad System:Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 Error !ClassiCube needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later (from PackMan)
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0.00 RMLoad System:Modules.ARMEABISupport
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0.00 Error !ClassiCube needs ARMEABISupport (from PackMan)
|
| Downloads (the game's sounds and textures on first run, the server
| list, signing in) are secure connections, made by the AcornSSL module
| (RISC OS 5.28 or later)
IfThere System:Modules.Network.URL.AcornSSL Then RMEnsure AcornSSL 0.00 RMLoad System:Modules.Network.URL.AcornSSL
|
| Downloads and sound run in their own threads: keep the thread timer's
| code safe in memory while other programs run
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 RMLoad <ClassiCube$Dir>.PThrTicker
|
| Sound: SharedSoundBuffer and StreamManager (ssb.zip from
| https://orac.co.uk/software/rdpclient/rdpclient.html) if they're there,
| otherwise DigitalRenderer
RMEnsure SharedSound 1.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSound Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSound
RMEnsure StreamManager 0.03 IfThere System:Modules.StreamMan Then RMLoad System:Modules.StreamMan
RMEnsure SharedSoundBuffer 0.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSBuffer Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSBuffer
RMEnsure SharedSoundBuffer 0.07 RMEnsure DigitalRenderer 0.51 IfThere System:Modules.DRenderer Then RMLoad System:Modules.DRenderer
|
| Drawing is done by the CPU, so the game draws at 640x360 and the picture
| is stretched to the window or screen (on a Raspberry Pi with VideoOverlay
| the display does that, for nothing). Set these before running to change:
|   ClassiCube$RenderSize  WxH (fewer pixels = faster), or full
|   ClassiCube$Overlay     0 to stretch without the overlay
|   ClassiCube$WindowSize  WxH (default: 3x, 2x or 1.5x the render size,
|                          the biggest that fits on the desktop)
If "<ClassiCube$RenderSize>" = "" Then Set ClassiCube$RenderSize 640x360
RMEnsure VideoOverlay 0.00 IfThere System:Modules.VideoOverlay Then RMLoad System:Modules.VideoOverlay
|
| Options, downloaded resources, maps, screenshots and texture packs
If "<ClassiCube$Data>" = "" Then Set ClassiCube$Data <Choices$Write>.ClassiCube
CDir <ClassiCube$Data>
|
| Messages go to a file instead of opening a command window
Set ALSOFT_LOGFILE <Wimp$ScrapDir>.ClassiCubeAL
|
| The program is about 13.6 MB (code and data); UnixLib keeps its heap in
| a dynamic area, so the slot only has to hold the program and some room
WimpSlot -min 20480K -max 20480K
Run <ClassiCube$Dir>.!RunImage > <Wimp$ScrapDir>.ClassiCubeLog 2>&1
